{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 28, :comments ["״סקול יסקל השור״ — according to the plain sense:" "״ולא יאכל את בשרו״ — not to a gentile and not to a dog after it has been stoned, even though nevelah and treifah are written about them — whether sold to a gentile or thrown to a dog, here it is not permitted for benefit after stoning. And the Sages explained: from the time its sentence is final it is forbidden, even if one slaughtered it after the final sentence." "״ובעל השור נקי״ — as long as it had not been warned."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:42:28.509029220Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}